{{!< default}}
{{#contentFor "moHead"}}
<title>Search The Faith Received</title>
<meta name="description" content="Search across every creed, confession, catechism, and classic work in The Faith Received: full text, by work, by tradition, and by passage." />
<meta property="og:title" content="Search The Faith Received" />
<meta property="og:description" content="Search across every creed, confession, catechism, and classic work in The Faith Received." />
<meta name="twitter:title" content="Search The Faith Received" />
<meta name="twitter:description" content="Search across every creed, confession, catechism, and classic work in The Faith Received." />
{{/contentFor}}
{{!-- /the-faith-received/search/ — six modes, one page, per the data
     owner's 2026-09-03 brief: Find, Ask, Full text, Meaning, Scripture,
     Tradition. Find/Full text/Tradition run on the real Pagefind index
     mirrored into the mo-tfr bucket at v1/search/pagefind/ (ten shards,
     ~108,500 pages of the Latin Library — see the header of
     assets/js/faith-tfr-search.js for how that was confirmed and how
     the shards are merged). Ask is real, built inline via a shared
     partial, see [data-fs-panel="ask"] below. The sixth tab was
     "Meaning" and is now Power Search: the semantic index it used to
     say did not exist does exist, and the tab is a door into the one
     place it lives rather than a second copy of it. See
     [data-fs-panel="power"] below.

     Rebuilt 2026-09-11 alongside a port from the corpus owner's own
     /search. What came across and what did not is written up in the
     header of assets/js/faith-tfr-search.js; the parts that show here
     are the Power Search tab, the start state and the zero state that
     the result panels now render, and the Preview control on each row.

     Fresh data-fs-* attributes throughout, deliberately not the older
     data-faith-search-* set assets/js/faith-received.js still binds
     to (a smaller, separate Fuse.js index over the ~100 native English
     Editions only) — so that dead code stays inert here rather than
     double-driving these same result lists. That script is not loaded
     on this page at all any more; see the script list at the bottom. --}}

<main class="faith-received faith-feature">

  <section class="bhero bhero--tool">
    <div class="bhero-inner container">
      <p class="bhero-kicker"><a href="/the-faith-received/">The Faith Received</a> <span aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span> <a href="/the-faith-received/search/">Search</a></p>
      <h1>Search</h1>
      {{!-- BETA GATE. Two subs, because the lede has to be true for
           whoever is reading it: "six ways in, below" over a signup box
           is a promise the page is not keeping at that moment. --}}
      {{#if @member}}
      <p class="bhero-sub">Search across every creed, confession, catechism, and work in the library. Six ways in, below.</p>

      <form class="faith-search-form" data-fs-form>
        <label class="visually-hidden" for="fs-query">Search The Faith Received</label>
        <input id="fs-query" type="search" data-fs-query autocomplete="off" placeholder="Search a word or phrase&hellip;" />
        <button type="submit" class="btn btn-primary">Search</button>
      </form>
      <p class="faith-search-status" data-fs-status role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
      {{else}}
      <p class="bhero-sub">Search across every creed, confession, catechism, and work in the library. All six ways in are free while the beta runs. Each one needs an account.</p>
      {{/if}}
    </div>
  </section>

  {{!-- BETA GATE, tools branch. Every mode on this page is a research
       tool, the search box in the hero above included, so the gate
       takes the whole apparatus rather than the two tabs that spend
       money. Nothing crawlable is lost: Find, Full text and Tradition
       render from Pagefind in the browser, so a crawler was never
       reading anything but this shell.

       The contract is in partials/faith-received/_beta-gate.hbs. --}}
  {{#if @member}}
  <section class="bband faith-feature-body">
    <div class="container container-narrow" data-fs-page>

      {{!-- Mode tabs. Markup/CSS pattern lifted from the Heidelberg
           view toggle (assets/css/faith-received.css, "View toggle
           (Heidelberg)") rather than inventing a new tab chrome. --}}
      <nav class="faith-view-toggle faith-search-modes" data-fs-tabs role="tablist" aria-label="Search mode">
        <button type="button" class="faith-view-toggle-tab is-active" data-fs-mode="find" role="tab" aria-selected="true">Find</button>
        <button type="button" class="faith-view-toggle-tab" data-fs-mode="fulltext" role="tab" aria-selected="false">Full text</button>
        {{!-- Works searches the NAME of a work. Every other tab here
             searches text, so a reader asking for a book by its title was
             the one thing this page could not answer. --}}
        <button type="button" class="faith-view-toggle-tab" data-fs-mode="works" role="tab" aria-selected="false">Works</button>
        <button type="button" class="faith-view-toggle-tab" data-fs-mode="tradition" role="tab" aria-selected="false">Tradition</button>
        <button type="button" class="faith-view-toggle-tab" data-fs-mode="scripture" role="tab" aria-selected="false">Scripture</button>
        <button type="button" class="faith-view-toggle-tab" data-fs-mode="ask" role="tab" aria-selected="false">Ask</button>
        {{!-- Was "Meaning", and was an honest placeholder for a feature
              that did not exist. It exists now and it is called Power
              Search, on /the-faith-received/research/. The tab is kept
              because this is where a reader looks for it, and the name
              is the product's name so the two agree. --}}
        <button type="button" class="faith-view-toggle-tab" data-fs-mode="power" role="tab" aria-selected="false">Power Search</button>
      </nav>

      {{!-- Shared scope filters — author / work / tradition — per the
           brief's "sharing scope filters" across modes. Same markup
           convention as the curated topic pages
           (partials/faith-received/_topic-*.hbs): .faith-topic-filters
           / .faith-filter-group / .faith-filter-pill.

           Hidden by CSS while the Ask tab is active (`.fs-page--ask
           .faith-search-scope`, set by faith-tfr-search.js's
           showMode()): ten pills plus two text inputs dominated
           everything below them, and Ask carries its own collapsed
           multi-select scope control inside its composer. Hidden, never
           cleared — these pills are single-select and drive Pagefind
           for the other five modes, and their state is exactly as it
           was left when you switch back. --}}
      <div class="faith-topic-filters faith-search-scope">
        <div class="faith-filter-group" data-fs-trad-group>
          <span class="faith-filter-label">Tradition</span>
          <button type="button" class="faith-filter-pill is-active" data-fs-trad="">All</button>
          <button type="button" class="faith-filter-pill" data-fs-trad="English Divines">English Divines</button>
          <button type="button" class="faith-filter-pill" data-fs-trad="Greek Fathers">Greek Fathers</button>
          <button type="button" class="faith-filter-pill" data-fs-trad="Humanism and Law">Humanism and Law</button>
          <button type="button" class="faith-filter-pill" data-fs-trad="Lutheran">Lutheran</button>
          <button type="button" class="faith-filter-pill" data-fs-trad="Medieval">Medieval</button>
          <button type="button" class="faith-filter-pill" data-fs-trad="Latin Fathers">Latin Fathers</button>
          <button type="button" class="faith-filter-pill" data-fs-trad="Eastern Fathers">Eastern Fathers</button>
          <button type="button" class="faith-filter-pill" data-fs-trad="Roman Catholic">Roman Catholic</button>
          <button type="button" class="faith-filter-pill" data-fs-trad="Reformed">Reformed</button>
        </div>
        <div class="faith-filter-group faith-search-scope-text">
          <label class="faith-search-scope-label">Author <input type="text" data-fs-author placeholder="e.g. Baxter" /></label>
          <label class="faith-search-scope-label">Work <input type="text" data-fs-work placeholder="e.g. Institutes" /></label>
        </div>
      </div>

      {{!-- Find: grouped by work, per the brief — "a hit lists the
           work once with its matching section headings under it, each
           with its page." --}}
      <div data-fs-panel="find">
        <p class="faith-search-status" data-fs-count="find" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
        <div data-fs-results="find"></div>
      </div>

      {{!-- Full text: the same index, flat, one row per matching page. --}}
      <div data-fs-panel="fulltext" hidden>
        <p class="faith-search-status" data-fs-count="fulltext" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
        <ol class="faith-search-results" data-fs-results="fulltext"></ol>
      </div>

      {{!-- Tradition: Full text with the Tradition pill pinned rather
           than optional. Uses the same pill row above; this panel just
           insists one is chosen before it runs anything. --}}
      {{!-- Works: find a book by its name, across all eight collections.
           Answered by GET /v1/titles on mo-tfr-library, which holds a
           slim prebuilt title index in the worker. The browser downloads
           none of it: the same index shipped to the client would be
           1,164 KB gzipped, and the titles are most of that, so there is
           no cheap shape of it. See lib/titles.js. --}}
      <div data-fs-panel="works" hidden>
        <p class="faith-search-status" data-fs-count="works" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
        <ol class="faith-search-results" data-fs-results="works"></ol>
      </div>

      <div data-fs-panel="tradition" hidden>
        <p class="faith-search-scope-note" data-fs-trad-required>Choose a tradition above to search within it.</p>
        <p class="faith-search-status" data-fs-count="tradition" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
        <ol class="faith-search-results" data-fs-results="tradition"></ol>
      </div>

      {{!-- Scripture: a passage-lookup shortcut into the full Scripture
           Index (/the-faith-received/scripture/), which already carries
           the canon-wide citation panel, the tradition filter chips, and
           the citation-density strip. Not a second citation browser. --}}
      <div class="faith-search-scripture-panel" data-fs-panel="scripture" hidden>
        <p class="faith-pending-note faith-search-scripture-note">Jump straight to a passage in the full Scripture Index, which carries every citation in the library, by book, with tradition filters and a canon-wide density chart.</p>
        <form class="faith-scripture-jump" data-fs-scripture-form>
          <label class="faith-scripture-jump-label"><span>Go to a passage</span>
            <input type="text" class="faith-scripture-jump-input" data-fs-scripture-input placeholder="Romans 8, or Genesis 1" aria-label="Go to a book and chapter">
          </label>
          <button type="submit" class="fa-search-btn">Go</button>
        </form>
        <p class="faith-search-status" data-fs-scripture-status role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
        <p class="faith-search-scripture-cta"><a class="btn btn-outline" href="/the-faith-received/scripture/">Open the full Scripture Index</a></p>
      </div>

      {{!-- Ask: built inline, not a link-out. Ask used to be reachable
           only from its own routed page (/the-faith-received/ask/) with
           this tab carrying a "Open Ask" placeholder pointing there —
           on the reasoning at the time that a second Ask UI bound to
           the same mo-tfr-library /v1/ask call was a second thing to
           keep in sync for no reader benefit. Rebuilt 2026-09 as a
           shared Handlebars partial instead
           (partials/faith-received/_ask-panel.hbs) so that reasoning no
           longer applies: this tab and the standalone /ask/ page both
           render the same partial, so there is still exactly one copy
           of the markup, but a reader on this page can now actually use
           Ask without leaving it. assets/js/page/faith-ask.js binds to
           the partial's markup with plain unscoped querySelector()
           calls, so it works here unchanged.

           .ask-workspace (in the partial) makes its own width: it
           breaks out of this page's `container-narrow` (720px) and
           runs the full width of the viewport, so the container no
           longer has to be widened for it. faith-tfr-search.js's
           showMode() still toggles `.fs-page--ask` on [data-fs-page]
           while this tab is active; that class now hides the shared
           scope row above instead of resizing the container, which
           also means the tab strip no longer jumps 460px wider the
           moment Ask is selected — see ".fs-page--ask" in
           faith-received.css. --}}
      <div data-fs-panel="ask" data-ask-page hidden>
        {{> "faith-received/_ask-panel"}}
      </div>
      {{!-- Power Search. This panel used to say that searching by
           meaning needed a vector index nobody had built, which was
           true when it was written and is not true now: Power Search
           ships on /the-faith-received/research/, talking to
           mo-tfr-library's GET /v1/vsearch over the Vectorize index
           (assets/js/page/faith-power-search.js is the authority on the
           query params and the result shape).

           It is a door, not a second copy. Power Search groups its
           results by work and opens each work's own passages from a
           second, slug-scoped query; rebuilding that here would be two
           of the same thing to keep in step, which is the mistake the
           Ask tab already made once. So this panel says what Power
           Search does, says plainly that it is for members, and links
           into the one place it lives. --}}
      <div data-fs-panel="power" hidden>
        <div class="faith-pending-panel faith-search-pending-panel">
          <p class="faith-pending-lede">Power Search finds a passage by what it means rather than by the words it uses.</p>
          <p class="faith-pending-note">Full text and Find match the words on the page. Power Search matches the sense, so a search for &ldquo;God&rsquo;s unchangeableness&rdquo; also reaches a passage that says immutability and never uses your word at all. Results come back a work at a time, and opening a work shows its own best passages underneath. It is one of the member tools in the Research workspace.</p>
          <p class="faith-pending-actions">
            <a href="/the-faith-received/research/#power-search">Open Power Search</a>
            <a href="/the-faith-received/search/#fulltext">Search the words instead</a>
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>
  {{/if}}

  {{> "faith-received/_beta-gate"}}

  {{!-- No prices here on purpose: /membership/ is where they live, and a
       number repeated in two places is a number that goes stale in one. --}}


<section class="faith-join">
  <div class="container">
    <p class="blabel">Become a member</p>
    <h2>Use the tools and support the work.</h2>
      <div class="toggle-wrap" role="tablist" aria-label="Billing interval">
        <div class="toggle">
          <button type="button" class="toggle-option is-active" data-interval="annual" role="tab" aria-selected="true" data-hm-goal="plan-annual">
            Annual
            <span class="badge">Save 17%</span>
          </button>
          <button type="button" class="toggle-option" data-interval="monthly" role="tab" aria-selected="false" data-hm-goal="plan-monthly">Monthly</button>
        </div>
      </div>
  </div>
</section>

{{> "membership-pricing"}}
{{> "faith-received/_beta-band"}}
</main>
{{!-- The sitewide membership CTA used to sit here. It was pulled on
     2026-09-11 by Ian: its copy is essay-specific ("Loved this essay?
     Help us write the next one"), which reads as nonsense at the foot
     of a research tool, and on this page it was the third membership
     pitch in a row. The merged band above already names what membership
     buys and says the tools become Member features after the beta, and
     the pricing cards sit between the two.

     It is STILL on the twenty browse, reading-room and shelf pages,
     where it is the only membership prompt there is. Those need a
     replacement written for a library rather than a deletion. --}}

<script src="{{asset "js/page/membership-toggle.js"}}"></script>
<script src="{{asset "js/page/membership-cards.js"}}"></script>

{{!-- Claims the TFR / TFR-Beta Kit tags for a signed-in member. Hides
     and reveals nothing; see the file header. --}}
<script src="{{asset "js/faith-beta-gate.js"}}"></script>

{{!-- The search scripts ride inside the same member branch as the
     markup they bind to. A signed-out visitor has no panels. --}}
{{#if @member}}
{{!-- Ask tab: same two scripts, in the same relative order, that
     custom-faith-ask.hbs loads for the same partial — feature-gate.js
     gates the submit button in partials/faith-received/_ask-panel.hbs,
     then page/faith-ask.js does the DOM binding. Both are plain
     page-bottom <script src> tags rather than bundle dependencies
     because page-template scripts run before site.min.js.

     The tier feature-gate.js enforces is a constant in that file. It is
     subscriber-tier for the beta and member-tier otherwise, so this
     comment deliberately does not name one. --}}
<script src="{{asset "js/feature-gate.js"}}"></script>
<script src="{{asset "js/port/ask-store.js"}}"></script>
<script src="{{asset "js/faith-ask-history.js"}}"></script>
<script src="{{asset "js/page/faith-ask.js"}}"></script>

{{!-- The six-mode search page itself: mode tabs, the Pagefind-backed
     Find/Full text/Tradition modes, and the Scripture shortcut. Loads
     no CDN script — the old fuse.js dependency went with the Fuse-based
     search this page no longer runs (see the file's own header). --}}
<script src="{{asset "js/faith-tfr-search.js"}}"></script>
{{/if}}
